<title>EGYPT: Upper Egypt Mills 10-mth results.</title>
<headline>Upper Egypt Mills 10-mth results.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Upper Egypt Flour Mills said on Friday it made profits of 56 million pounds ($16.5 million) in the first 10 months of the financial year 1996/7, against 38 million in the same period of 1995/6. The years start July 1.</p>
<p>In the whole of 1995/6 it made a net attributable profit of 43.104 million pounds.</p>
<p>The company said it was studying offers from international companies to set up a 72 percent extraction flour mill in Sixth of October City in conjunction with the public-sector company General Greater Cairo Bakeries. The mill would generate revenue of 25 million pounds a year, it said.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
